      "writtenOn": "2019-02-22T01:49:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It might just be me, but I\u0027d need it spelled out more that use of authorization scopes is a fundamental shift from the legacy way of doing things. That is, instead of an API that adjusts its behavior based on a fine-grained/complex custom policy.json configured by an operator, we have an API that adjusts its behavior based on the token scope it was called with and simpler or non-existent custom policy.json.\n\nAnd that end users need to be educated about how to set up roles with scopes and request different token scopes in Keystone before calling our API.",
      "revId": "21d81f46f88aa4cc1f42bd6b026af81c9c8af7e2",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
